From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cube oakley <cube-oakley@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 02:39:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] cpif: build on Linux 7.3 (Kbuild, void remove,
 class_create, pde_data, strscpy, timers, hrtimer_setup, dummy netdevs, napi
 weight, GRO_DROP, WQ_PERCPU, of_get_named_gpio)

- Kbuild: cpif.ko, shm_ipc.ko and cpif_page.ko with the S5100/PCIe
  configuration as -DCONFIG_* flags.
- s51xx_pcie.h takes the root-complex API from the stand-in header
  instead of extern declarations.
- of_get_named_gpio() and <linux/of_gpio.h> are gone: a local
  cpif_of_get_named_gpio() resolves the phandle's GPIO chip by fwnode and
  returns the legacy number, so the rest keeps the integer GPIO API.
- Dummy NAPI netdevs are allocated (alloc_netdev_dummy) instead of
  embedded, and freed on the create error paths.
- strncpy/strlcpy: strscpy(_pad); the CP boot log is read with
  memcpy_fromio and terminated.
- napi_gro_receive() no longer reports GRO_DROP.
- mem_rx_work stays per-CPU (WQ_PERCPU), as the 5.10 default was.
- <linux/stdarg.h>, <linux/panic_notifier.h>, void platform remove,
  class_create(name), pde_data(), timer_delete(), timer_container_of(),
  hrtimer_setup(), netif_napi_add_weight().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
